---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const [profile] = await getCollection('profile');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Both Sides of the Discount Moved — Braeden Keena"
  description="A 9,077-facility longitudinal pricing study. Daily exact-listing snapshots show reference rates rising a median of $45 on the same day 40%-off promotions were assigned."
>
  <Nav name={profile.data.name} />

  <article class="study-page">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <header class="study-header">
        <div class="study-kicker-row">
          <span class="study-kicker">Storage Price Observatory · Longitudinal Pricing Investigation</span>
          <span class="study-badge">9,077 Facilities · 129,704 Daily SKUs</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="study-title">Both Sides of the Discount Moved.</h1>
        <p class="study-provenance">
          A finding from the <strong>Storage Price Observatory</strong>. The Public Storage series
          is continuous from 29 April 2026; the six other collections were added during September
          2026. Through 25 August that Public Storage collection was published as a directory called
          <a href="/work/findstorage">FindStorage</a> — a product since retired, whose headline
          figures are frozen at that date and reported separately from the figures here.
        </p>
        <p class="study-lede">
          A percentage-off advertisement contains two numbers: the stated discount and the baseline rate used to calculate savings. 
          When daily snapshots followed exact listings through time, both numbers moved together:
          reference rates rose by a median of $45 on the same day "40% off" discounts appeared, and when rates were later cut, roughly half the promotional value was withdrawn alongside them — leaving modeled four-month cost slightly higher than before.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Top Hard Stats Grid -->
      <div class="stat-banner">
        <!-- Event 1: 1 August Reference-Rate Hike -->
        <div class="stat-group">
          <div class="stat-group__header">
            <span class="stat-group__tag">1 August</span>
            <span class="stat-group__title">Reference-rate increase assigned with promotion</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-group__cards">
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num">4,904 / 4,904</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">1 August listings entering the promo that also received a rate hike</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__sub">0 / 428 in 28 July control (0.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num text-alert">+$45</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">median reference-rate increase, same day the 40%-off was assigned</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Event 2: 14 September Portfolio Reset -->
        <div class="stat-group stat-group--conclusion">
          <div class="stat-group__header">
            <span class="stat-group__tag">14 September</span>
            <span class="stat-group__title">Headline rate cut and promotional withdrawal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-group__cards">
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num">−14.7%</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">rates fell, across 59,045 exact-matched modelable listings, 14 Sept</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-banner__card stat-banner__card--featured">
              <span class="stat-banner__tag">The Net Outcome</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__num text-alert">+1.1%</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">modeled four-month cost to the customer — higher, despite the rate cut</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__sub">promotional discount value withdrawn: −49.7%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- VISUAL 1: the 28 July control against the 1 August event -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">The Smoking Gun · Physical Control</span>
          <h2>The Control That Proves It Wasn't a System Glitch</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Could a website update engine simply bundle rate and promo updates together? 
            July supplies the empirical control. Four days before August 1, hundreds of listings rotated into the same discount with zero rate hikes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-grid">
          <!-- July 28 Control -->
          <div class="evidence-panel">
            <div class="evidence-panel__top">
              <span class="evidence-date">July 28, 2026</span>
              <span class="evidence-tag">The Control</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-stat">
              <strong>0 / 428</strong>
              <span>promo entrants received a rate increase (0.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-bar-track">
              <div class="evidence-bar-fill" style="width: 0%;"></div>
            </div>
            <p class="evidence-note">
              428 listings entered "40% off For 4 Months". Rates remained completely flat. Proves rate and promo fields are independently writable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- August 1 Event -->
          <div class="evidence-panel evidence-panel--alert">
            <div class="evidence-panel__top">
              <span class="evidence-date">August 1, 2026</span>
              <span class="evidence-tag evidence-tag--alert">The Coordinated Wave</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-stat">
              <strong class="text-alert">4,904 / 4,904</strong>
              <span>promo entrants received an immediate rate increase (100.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-bar-track">
              <div class="evidence-bar-fill evidence-bar-fill--alert" style="width: 100%;"></div>
            </div>
            <p class="evidence-note text-alert">
              Every single listing entering the 4-month promo had its reference rate increased on the exact same morning. Median hike: +$45.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 2: Costa Mesa — how the advertised savings figure was calculated -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">Exact Listing Reconstruction</span>
          <h2>Anatomy of an Advertised "Savings" Figure</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Tracking Costa Mesa facility #235 (Unit 5x15) through daily snapshots shows the reference rate elevated on 22 and 24 August and back down on the 25th — with the "$380 Savings" claim calculated against it on the 24th.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- SVG Timeline Chart -->
        <div class="chart-container">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 280" class="svg-chart" role="img" aria-label="Timeline chart of Costa Mesa store rate jumps">
            <!-- Background Grid lines -->
            <line x1="80" y1="40" x2="760" y2="40" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="45" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$240</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="110" x2="760" y2="110" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="115" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$200</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="180" x2="760" y2="180" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="185" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$160</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="230" x2="760" y2="230" stroke="var(--border)" />
            <text x="65" y="235" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$130</text>

            <!-- Day markers & vertical lines -->
            <!-- Aug 20 -->
            <line x1="160" y1="40" x2="160" y2="230" stroke="var(--border-soft)" />
            <text x="160" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 20</text>

            <!-- Aug 22 (Jump) -->
            <line x1="320" y1="40" x2="320" y2="230" stroke="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.2)" />
            <text x="320" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 22</text>

            <!-- Aug 24 (The Ad) -->
            <line x1="480" y1="40" x2="480" y2="230" stroke="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.4)" stroke-dasharray="3" />
            <text x="480" y="250" fill="#d97706" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Aug 24 (Ad)</text>

            <!-- Aug 25 (Reversal) -->
            <line x1="640" y1="40" x2="640" y2="230" stroke="var(--border-soft)" />
            <text x="640" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 25</text>

            <!-- Reference Rate Line: 161 -> 161 -> 237 -> 237 -> 161 -->
            <path d="M 100 178 L 220 178 L 320 45 L 540 45 L 640 178 L 740 178" fill="none" stroke="#e05252" stroke-width="3" />

            <!-- Net Rent Paid Line: 161 -> 161 -> 142 -> 142 -> 161 -->
            <path d="M 100 178 L 220 178 L 320 212 L 540 212 L 640 178 L 740 178" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />

            <!-- Highlight Dots -->
            <!-- Baseline Aug 20: 161 -->
            <circle cx="160" cy="178" r="5" fill="#e05252" />
            <text x="160" y="165" fill="#e05252" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">$161 Baseline</text>

            <!-- Spike Aug 24: 237 -->
            <circle cx="480" cy="45" r="6" fill="#e05252" />
            <text x="480" y="32" fill="#e05252" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">$237 Struck-Through Reference Rate (+47%)</text>

            <!-- Promo payment: 142 -->
            <circle cx="480" cy="212" r="6" fill="var(--accent)" />
            <text x="480" y="200" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">$142 Promotional Rate (40% off $237)</text>

            <!-- Savings delta bracket / callout -->
            <line x1="560" y1="45" x2="570" y2="45" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <line x1="570" y1="45" x2="570" y2="212" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <line x1="560" y1="212" x2="570" y2="212" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="585" y="132" fill="#d97706" font-size="12" font-weight="700">4 × $95/mo = "$380 SAVINGS!"</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- The Breakdown Table -->
        <div class="breakdown-grid">
          <div class="breakdown-card">
            <h4>What the Customer Saw on Screen</h4>
            <div class="ad-mockup">
              <span class="ad-tag">Month 1–4 · 40% OFF</span>
              <div class="ad-price">
                <s class="ad-strike">$237 / mo</s>
                <strong class="ad-deal">$142.20 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="ad-claim">★ Total Estimated 12-Month Savings: <strong>$380</strong><br><small>The figure is exactly four months at 40% off the displayed reference rate: 4 × ($237 − $142.20) = $379.20.</small></div>
            </div>
            <p class="breakdown-note">
              The arithmetic is correct <em>only if you accept that the unit actually cost $237</em>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="breakdown-card breakdown-card--truth">
            <h4>What the Longitudinal Pipeline Caught</h4>
            <div class="math-breakdown">
              <div class="math-row">
                <span>Steady-state street price (Aug 20 & Aug 25):</span>
                <strong>$161.00 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row">
                <span>Renter pays during promo window:</span>
                <strong>$142.20 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row highlight-delta">
                <span>Real 4-month savings ($161.00 − $142.20) × 4:</span>
                <strong class="text-accent">~$75.20</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row highlight-phantom">
                <span>Phantom savings from temporary rate hike:</span>
                <strong class="text-alert">~$304.80</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="breakdown-note">
              <strong>80.2% of the advertised savings figure rests on the elevated reference rate</strong> rather than on any change in what the unit cost on the days either side of it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 3: The September 14 Trade & Shapley Decomposition -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">The September Unwind · Portfolio Modeling</span>
          <h2>The "Rate Cut" That Quietly Raised Consumer Costs</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            On September 14, headline rates fell across the portfolio — no announcement was made; the change was observed in the daily snapshot.
            Across 59,045 exact-matched modelable listings, rates fell 14.7%. 
            At the same time roughly half the promotional value was withdrawn, leaving modeled four-month cost on matched offers slightly <strong>higher</strong> than before.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="waterfall-container">
          <div class="waterfall-bars">
            <div class="wf-bar">
              <span class="wf-val down">−15.4%</span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--down" style="height: 110px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label">Rate Cut Impact<br><small>Lower monthly rent</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-sign">+</div>
            <div class="wf-bar">
              <span class="wf-val up">+16.5%</span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--up" style="height: 118px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label">Promo Slash Impact<br><small>Withdrawn discounts</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-sign">=</div>
            <div class="wf-bar wf-bar--result">
              <span class="wf-val up"><strong>+1.1%</strong></span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--result" style="height: 24px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label"><strong>Net Customer Cost</strong><br><small>Modeled 4-month spend</small></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="wf-caption">
            <strong>Shapley decomposition of the 14 September reset:</strong> 
            Looking at headline rates alone describes a customer windfall. Looking at both fields together describes something else:
            the rate reduction and the promotional withdrawal are close to the same size, and they point in opposite directions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 4: Tested in Public — The Living Ledger & September 18 Walkback -->
      <section class="visual-card visual-card--ledger">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <div class="ledger-pill">LIVING LEDGER AUDIT · 18 SEPTEMBER 2026</div>
          <h2>The Reset Walkback: Caught Live 96 Hours Later</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Had our study frozen on September 14, it would have claimed Public Storage locked in a 25% lower rate regime entering Q4. 
            The daily pipeline stayed online. On <strong>18 September 2026</strong>, Public Storage restored roughly 12% across 22,772 units, rewriting 17,935 promotions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Matched Panel Index SVG -->
        <div class="panel-index-box">
          <div class="index-metric">
            <span class="index-metric__lbl">Matched Panel Index (13 Sept = 1.0000)</span>
            <span class="index-metric__num">0.9800</span>
            <span class="index-metric__sub">Only 2% below starting rate, not 25%</span>
          </div>

          <div class="index-timeline">
            <div class="tl-node">
              <span class="tl-date">13 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val">1.0000</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Baseline</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--down">
              <span class="tl-date">14 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val text-alert">0.7667</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Coordinated reset · 31,244 price events</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--sealed">
              <span class="tl-date">15 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val">0.7667</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Predictions sealed · 74 price events</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--restored">
              <span class="tl-date">18 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val text-accent">0.9800</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">+12% Restored (22k units)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: The Sealed Predictions -->
      <section class="study-section">
        <h2>The Pre-Registered Prediction (Sealed 15 September 2026)</h2>
        <p>
          Public Storage reports Q3 in late October. The three predictions below were sealed in commit <code>2026-09-15-q3-prediction-and-ledger-gap.md</code> before results exist.
        </p>

        <div class="pred-grid">
          <div class="pred-item">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P1 · Primary</div>
            <h3>Q3 Promotional Discounts Given</h3>
            <p>Q2 2026 reported promo discounts up 16.1% YoY. Following summer discounting and the September contraction:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P1:</strong> Q3 promotional discounts will still be up YoY, but growth rate will decelerate below +16.1%.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pred-item">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P2 · Primary</div>
            <h3>Q3 New-Customer Contract Rates</h3>
            <p>Q2 reported new contract rates up 1.6% YoY (first positive reading since 2021). Weighting pre vs post reset days:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P2:</strong> Q3 new-customer contract rate growth will come in below +1.6% YoY.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pred-item pred-item--counter">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P3 · Counter-Guidance Bet</div>
            <h3>Q4 New-Customer Contract Rates</h3>
            <p>Management guided move-in rents to positive low single digits. Our daily volatility and demand models indicate:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P3:</strong> Q4 new-customer contract rates will be flat or negative YoY, directly contradicting company guidance.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Dual Doors to the Full Engine -->
      <section class="doors-section">
        <div class="doors-header">
          <span class="doors-eyebrow">Inspect the Data & Tools</span>
          <h2>The Heavy Lifting Lives in the Live Engine</h2>
          <p class="doors-desc">
            This teardown summarizes the core findings. For the complete mathematical proofs, raw accounting tables, and national market coverage, dive straight into the rate monitor:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doors-grid">
          <!-- Door 1: Case Study & Econometric Proof (#study) -->
          <div class="door-card door-card--study">
            <div class="door-card__top">
              <span class="door-badge door-badge--study">Econometric Proof</span>
              <span class="door-hash">#study</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Full Methodology & 59k-Offer Accounting</h3>
            <p class="door-text">
              The rigorous academic writeup with complete before-and-after tables, Shapley decomposition arithmetic, and multi-unit Costa Mesa verification.
            </p>
            <ul class="door-bullets">
              <li><strong>59,045 matched listings</strong> in the four-month accounting ledger ($32.78M → $27.96M headline, $10.20M → $5.13M promo)</li>
              <li><strong>77 of 92</strong> days observed across Q3 with zero synthetic interpolation (including the deliberate 26–30 August terms review pause)</li>
              <li><strong>Full multi-unit breakdown</strong> for 5×5, 5×10, and 5×15 SKUs</li>
              <li><strong>Legal boundary note</strong> and analytical portfolio methodology</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/storage/dashboard.html#study" class="door-btn door-btn--study">
              Open Full Methodology & Data Tables (#study) →
            </a>
          </div>

          <!-- Door 2: Live Market Observatory (#overview) -->
          <div class="door-card door-card--monitor">
            <div class="door-card__top">
              <span class="door-badge door-badge--monitor">Live Market Tool</span>
              <span class="door-hash">#overview</span>
            </div>
            <h3>7-Supplier National Rate Monitor</h3>
            <p class="door-text">
              Interactive GIS mapping and market intelligence across 9,077 facilities and 129,704 daily SKUs from America's top storage operators.
            </p>
            <ul class="door-bullets">
              <li><strong>Interactive Leaflet Map:</strong> store-level inventory & rate curves</li>
              <li><strong>7-Operator Benchmark:</strong> Public Storage, Extra Space, CubeSmart, Life Storage, NSA, Simply, U-Haul</li>
              <li><strong>Unit Size Pricing:</strong> 5×5 to 10×30 medians and interquartile ranges</li>
              <li><strong>Live Movers Feed:</strong> daily price hikes and cuts logged nationally</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/storage/dashboard.html#overview" class="door-btn door-btn--monitor">
              Launch National Rate Monitor Dashboard →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer profile={profile} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .study-page {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px);
  }

  .study-header {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .study-kicker-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .study-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .study-badge {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2px 10px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .study-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.5vw, 4.2rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    font-weight: 750;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .study-lede {
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Names the dataset and its boundary, so no reader fuses these figures with
     the retired FindStorage set. The 25 August 2026 line is a naming rule, not
     a pause: the two projects never share a count. */
  .study-provenance {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* Stat Banner */
  .stat-banner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-block: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .stat-banner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }

  .stat-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .stat-group__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }

  .stat-group__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--border-soft);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .stat-group--conclusion .stat-group__tag {
    background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.15);
    color: #d97706;
  }

  .stat-group__title {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .stat-group__cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .stat-group__cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .stat-banner__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .stat-banner__card--featured {
    border-color: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.45);
    background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.06);
    position: relative;
  }

  .stat-banner__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: #d97706;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: -2px;
  }

  .stat-banner__num {
    font-size: 1.85rem;
